Description:
    Adds a dropdown multi-select for a has_many :through association onto a
    resource that hibiki:rails:scaffold_controller already generated.

    Owner and Target must exist and be migrated. Join is required only when
    the owner doesn't declare the association yet — the join model and its
    migration are generated (belongs_to pair, touch: on the owner side, a
    unique index over the pair), and the has_many :through is injected into
    the owner.

    The channel gains one `include`; everything else lives in a generated
    concern under app/channels/concerns that wraps build_graph/list_locals
    with super. The selection is owned by the graph (the form's <target>_ids
    signal), so filtering the option list can never drop hidden selections.

    The option list is capped (OPTIONS_LIMIT in the concern, --limit to
    choose it); the cap is dropped under --skip-search, where it would strand
    the options it hides. Scaffolds generated before 0.7.0 lack the extras:
    hash the view rides on — it is threaded through their partials
    automatically.

Examples:
    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:multiselect Album Song Track

    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:multiselect Album Song --skip-search

    bin/rails g hibiki:rails:multiselect Album Song Track --label=name --limit=25
